Source: pg-circuit
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/PG-Circuit/pg-circuit

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-circuit
Architecture: any
Depends: ${postgresql:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Runtime protection against dangerous PostgreSQL statements
 PG Circuit Community inspects SQL statements and can observe, warn or
 block risky DML and DDL operations. Enable pg_circuit in
 shared_preload_libraries and restart PostgreSQL before use.
 Community reports runtime pressure but does not automatically change modes.
